test/**
.git/**
.gitignore
*.vsix

# Working notes, not the extension: the SDD ledger of a plan, the plans and
# specs themselves, and the guidance file addressed to Claude rather than to
# anyone installing this. Leaving them in took the package from 75 KB to 419 KB.
.superpowers/**
docs/**
CLAUDE.md

# Repository furniture and the screenshot harness: they belong on GitHub, not in
# an installed extension.
.github/**
tools/**

# Instructions addressed to Claude working on this repository — a skill for
# publishing, a model pin — not to anyone installing it. This was missed until
# 0.30.0, which shipped the publishing skill to both storefronts: a published
# version cannot be replaced, only unpublished, so it stays there and this line
# is what keeps the next one clean.
.claude/**

# Inside a .vsix everything lives under `extension/`, so unzipping one into the
# repository leaves a directory of that name — and the next `vsce package` packs
# it back in, shipping a second copy of whatever was in it. Caught once at 190 KB
# against the usual 143.
extension/**

# The marketplace listing pulls its screenshots from raw.githubusercontent, so
# the images live in git and stay out of the package — only the images the editor
# itself loads have to ship: the extension icon, the Activity Bar glyph, and the
# two theme halves of the title-bar button, all of which the editor resolves from
# `package.json` at runtime and draws as blank if they are not there.
media/**
!media/icon.png
!media/icon.svg
!media/bar-icon.svg
!media/open-claude-dark.svg
!media/open-claude-light.svg

# The terminal status line and the module behind it. Claude Code runs the script
# from the repository clone: the installed path carries the version number, so a
# `statusLine` command pointing into an installed .vsix breaks on the next
# update. The editor never loads either file.
bin/**
terminal.js
